WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:12.530
[Narrator:] In an effort to determine the vulnerability of coastal installations BW-attacked from offshore,

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.570
tests were held recently at a large airbase.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.210
The site selected was ideally suited to a test of this nature.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.920
Located on the coast, this vital military installation

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.340
is bordered by water on two sides.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.020
Two men ostensibly on a fishing trip,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.210
arrange to rent a small outboard motorboat.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.200
After receiving instructions in operating the boat,

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.170
the fishermen cast off.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.200
Once out of sight of the pier,

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.810
they made for an isolated spot on the shore.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:52.150
Here a disseminating device filled with a harmless BW agent

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.560
was put in the boat.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.600
The disseminating device and its power source were concealed under a tarpaulin.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:06.500
Then the man began an apparently aimless cruise up the bayou toward the airbase.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.500
With weather conditions favorable,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.730
the men begin to spray the dry simulant agent across the path

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.740
of a gentle wind blowing toward the airbase.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:22.820
Spraying was continuous while the boat traveled a distance of one and a half miles.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.090
In the immediate vicinity of the boat,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.670
the cloud of biological organisms could not be distinguished

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.540
from the exhaust smoke of the motor,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.650
and it rapidly became invisible as it drifted downwind.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.420
The wind of about three to six miles per hour

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.610
carried the cloud of simulant agent over most of the operations area,

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:48.260
administrative area, and base housing,

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.580
and continued in high concentration several miles beyond.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.010
At no time during the operation were the men challenged, questioned,

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.410
or even suspected of being other than fishermen.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.150
Certainly there was no outward indication that the airbase

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:10.820
was the target of a biological warfare attack.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.810
Had this been an actual attack with an infectious agent,

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:19.600
a tremendous patient load would have been imposed on the medical facilities.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.950
The operations of the base would have been seriously hampered,

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.840
or possibly even completely disrupted.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:27.830
In another test,

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:32.370
a similar type of disseminating device loaded with simulant agent was fitted

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.430
into the luggage compartment of an automobile

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.290
and connected to the exhaust pipe of the car.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:42.770
The operating controls of the unit were placed on the front seat,

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:46.900
so that the driver could easily start and stop the dissemination,

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.730
and vary the rate of output to suit the speed of the car.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.950
Driven along a public road upwind of the airbase,

00:02:54.970 --> 00:03:00.960
the vehicle appeared no different from any other car with a slightly smoky exhaust.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.170
No one paid any attention to the car, the driver,

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:11.040
or to the exhaust which in fact was a BW aerosol drifting toward the airbase.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:15.070
Applying the results of this test to a large, densely populated city

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.290
such as Washington, the tremendous casualty producing-potential

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:23.640
of biological warfare becomes frightening.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:28.830
And it would be so easy to contaminate the air with infectious organisms.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.770
These disseminating devices were merely jury-rigged affairs,

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:40.490
easily duplicated with parts attainable in any city.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:46.820
[BW DEVELOPMENT]

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.590
[Narrator:] At the U.S. Army Chemical Corps proving ground,

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:53.000
tests were conducted using an F-100 aircraft

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.830
equipped with an experimental spray device

00:03:55.850 --> 00:04:00.250
developed by one of the large aviation companies.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:03.920
One purpose of these tests was to establish the feasibility

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.550
of producing BW aerosols in the most effective

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:14.350
particle-size range as a low-level line source from high-speed aircraft.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.220
Wind-tunnel tests had shown that effective aerosols

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:25.060
could be produced by discharging the BW agent into a high-velocity airstream.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.470
To confirm the wind-tunnel test data,

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:33.910
an aerial mission was conducted using a BW-incapacitating agent.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.820
Flying at subsonic speed,

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:40.900
the F-100 disseminated the liquid agent along a 15-mile line

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.960
upwind of the test grid.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:47.580
Data from these tests were used to determine the effective coverage

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.980
that could be expected with an operational-type spray system,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.190
employing the basic principles of the experimental device.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:01.640
This study showed that one fighter aircraft flying on the deck

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.790
and dispensing two wing-tanks of a liquid BW agent

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.330
would cause infection in more than 50 percent of the populace

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:15.610
in an area 125 miles long by 30 miles deep.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.160
Three large aircraft could release sufficient agent

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.580
to infect over 50 percent of the people

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:26.180
in an area equivalent to a belt 140 miles wide,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.260
extending from New York to Chicago,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:39.950
comparable to the total area of Pennsylvania, Ohio, and Indiana.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:46.360
[VOLUNTEER EXPOSURE TO A BW AGENT]

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.060
[Narrator:] Volunteers and test animals were exposed in the field

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.960
to a mildly incapacitating BW agent.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:59.700
Aerosol generators were located on a line several thousand feet upwind

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:04.020
from the groups of men and animals.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:09.190
When preparations were complete the generators were fired.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:15.970
Even though the volunteers could not see, taste, or smell the aerosol as it drifted by,

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:19.490
they later developed symptoms typical of the disease

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:24.490
as a result of inhaling the infectious organisms.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:30.650
As each subject developed the characteristic fever, therapy was instituted.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:39.340
All responded to treatment and recovered completely.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:46.010
[CW DEVELOPMENTS...]

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:49.670
[Narrator:] This laboratory test demonstrates the casualty effect

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:57.520
of a non-persistent nerve gas developed by the United States Army Chemical Warfare laboratories.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.550
A healthy rabbit is placed in a sealed chamber

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:04.850
containing a small amount of the toxic gas.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:08.850
The clock timer on the wall indicates the number of seconds

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:12.910
the animal has been exposed to the gas.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:16.160
The chemical agent rapidly begins to take effect

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:21.840
and in 55 seconds the animal is incapacitated.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:24.880
The amount of gas used in this test was equivalent

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:32.540
to only one drop of the chemical in liquid form.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:38.430
The chemical acts on the nervous system and causes respiratory failure.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:42.740
Death occurred after the animal had been exposed to the gas

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:48.800
for two minutes and fifteen seconds.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:52.990
In the field, goats have been exposed to concentrations

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:57.260
of the agent from a gas field artillery shell.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.670
The test animals were placed in a trench

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:05.820
to protect them from the fragmentation and blast effects of the artillery round.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.580
One of the goats had been fitted with a protective mask.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:14.720
A 1-5-5 millimeter howitzer mounted on a tower

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:19.510
was aimed at the center of the circular target area.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:25.980
After the howitzer had been loaded and test personnel had retreated to a safe distance,

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:32.240
the weapon was fired by remote control.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:34.650
One minute after the shell exploded,

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:39.710
the animals were incapacitated by the effects of the gas.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:44.240
Some of the animals were dead after five minutes,

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:46.120
and within 15 minutes,

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:56.120
all had expired except the goat having the mask.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:01.730
Similar field tests were made with animals placed inside a tank.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:07.140
Here again, one of the goats was protected with a mask.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.700
In contrast to the earlier test,

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.240
a gas shell of small caliber was used,

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:18.940
and the amount of agent released was of course much less.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.480
Five minutes after the shell detonated against the tank,

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:28.700
the unmasked animals were dead from the effects of the gas.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.630
This test is an example of how toxic gas

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.500
can be used to penetrate enclosed places

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:41.820
and attack personnel protected in hard targets.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:44.060
The destructive action of the nerve gases

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.770
can be illustrated by a few simple sketches.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:56.020
This represents a normal nerve ending and this a normal muscle.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.430
The transmission of an impulse from the nerve ending

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:02.810
to the muscle involves the liberation of tiny quantities

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:10.540
of a chemical called acetylcholine, which triggers a muscle action.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:14.330
After a nerve-directed muscle contraction,

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:21.040
the enzyme cholinesterase almost immediately inactivates the acetylcholine,

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.800
permitting the muscle to relax again,

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:30.140
and thus the muscle action is terminated.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.930
Nerve gases knock out cholinesterase,

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:39.280
allowing an excess of acetylcholine to accumulate.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:43.030
As a result, the stimulation to muscle action

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:47.440
by acetylcholine becomes uncontrolled.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:51.770
And the neutralizing or relaxing effect of cholinesterase

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.800
becomes less and less,

00:10:53.820 --> 00:11:00.070
depending upon the severity of the nerve gas exposure.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:05.570
The drug atropine, long used in medicine as a pre-anesthetic agent,

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:09.840
can block the effects of accumulated acetylcholine

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:14.260
and thereby help to control muscle stimulation.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:24.450
Thus, atropine can prevent the destructive action of nerve gases.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:30.700
[Mental Incapacitators--PSYCHOCHEMICALS]

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.460
The psychochemicals, or K agents, being developed by the chemical corps

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:39.660
comprise a new family of incapacitating agents.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.620
These non-lethal chemicals have an astonishing capacity

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:49.040
to cause abnormal behavior in man and animals.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.720
In laboratory experiments a normal cat displays

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:55.970
the typical hunter instinct toward a mouse.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:12:01.250
A minute quantity of lysergic acid diethylamide, LSD,

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:04.690
is administered in aerosol form.

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:08.150
This chemical begins to react on the brain,

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:14.640
and after 45 seconds the effects of the psychochemical become apparent.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:18.170
The cat is no longer interested in catching the mouse,

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:21.450
and in fact appears to be afraid of it.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:25.240
Just a small quantity of LSD is sufficient to upset

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:32.220
the normal physical and emotional behavior pattern.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:35.780
To observe the effects of the psychochemical on humans,

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:41.390
enlisted volunteers were asked to take part in a carefully controlled test.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:42.420
Prior to the test,

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:45.260
the men behaved in a well-disciplined manner,

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:51.310
responding promptly to commands and executing movements with precision.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:55.980
During a break, each of the volunteers, except the drill sergeant,

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.110
received a minute dose of the psychochemical in coffee,

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:05.670
and about 30 minutes later the squad was ordered to fall in.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:09.340
Now the response of the men is entirely different.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:14.750
They have ceased to be alert, but have become relaxed and carefree.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.390
They cannot control the impulse to laugh,

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:23.100
and they no longer behave like well disciplined-troops.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:26.680
The drill sergeant has not received any of the psychochemical

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.720
and he issues commands as before.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:34.120
But the response of the men is sluggish and their movements ragged.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:39.670
They have become confused, irrational, and uncontrollable.

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.690
Seeing the effects of this chemical compound,

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:46.630
it is not difficult to imagine the habit that could be created

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:54.290
among weapons crews and command headquarters in time of war.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.010
In the continuing search for incapacitating agents,

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.390
the chemical warfare laboratories are investigating

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.630
a great many chemical compounds.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:12.510
One of these, CS4640, is of particular interest as a potential incapacitator.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:19.500
A very small amount of this compound produces partial paralysis in laboratory animals.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.390
The amount required is indicated in this comparison

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:25.860
with an ordinary aspirin tablet.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:29.070
The two dogs to be used in this test have been exposed

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:33.330
to effective doses of the chemical in previous tests

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.650
and have always recovered completely.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:41.000
A dilute solution of CS4640 is prepared for use

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:46.720
in creating an aerosol of the chemical in an exposure chamber.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:50.390
Although exposure to aerosol for about thirty seconds

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.970
is sufficient for the chemical to take effect,

00:14:53.990 --> 00:15:00.020
in this test the dogs will breath the aerosol for one minute.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:04.770
Exposure began at O900 hours.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.060
In numerous experiments,

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:11.520
temporary paralysis has been produced in a variety of laboratory animals:

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:19.060
mice, rats, guinea pigs, rabbits, cats, dogs, goats, and monkeys.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.160
After one minute,

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:24.260
the dogs were removed from the exposure chamber.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:29.250
On animals, the effect of a small dose of CS4640

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:34.340
is similar to that of a very much larger dose of morphine.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:38.300
It paralyzes the skeletal muscles.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:42.310
Depending on the size of the dose in relation to the weight of the animal,

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:48.280
the paralysis can be made to last from one to several hours.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:52.100
About ten minutes after the chemical had taken full effect,

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:57.190
the black dog was given an injection of an antidote.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.160
A couple of minutes later,

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.710
the paralysis had disappeared,

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:05.130
and the black dog was normal again.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:10.040
Without treatment, the other dog remained paralyzed.

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:14.840
The paralysis produced by the exposure to CS4640

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:19.290
for one minute lasted one hour,

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:23.280
after which the brown dog recovered.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:27.940
This incapacitating chemical compound is still in the research stage,

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:39.060
and no data are yet available as to its effects on humans.

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:44.860
[CW DEFENSE]

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:47.340
[Narrator:] Against the effects of toxic chemicals,

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.140
the protective mask has always been

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:52.410
the most important piece of individual equipment.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:56.960
It fully protects the delicate respiratory tract.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:01.360
But there are several chemical agents which have a percutaneous effect.

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:07.650
By absorption through the skin they can cause casualties or even death.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.430
Nerve gases are so toxic that a very small amount of the liquid

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:16.110
in contact with the skin can have a casualty effect.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.000
For these, the protective mask alone is not sufficient.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:23.580
The whole body must be protected with combat clothing,

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.980
which has been specially treated.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.750
After exposure to chemical attack,

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:33.710
even though protective clothing and masks are worn,

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:40.850
further precautionary action may be necessary to prevent casualties.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:46.060
For this purpose, an individual decontamination and treatment kit, E21,

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.480
has been developed.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.160
A dusting bag contains a decontaminating chemical

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:56.980
and a small capsule of agent-indicating dye.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.910
By crushing and kneading,

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.590
the capsule is broken

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:06.150
and the dye indicator is intimately mixed with the dusting powder.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:08.590
The decontaminating powder will neutralize

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:12.860
small droplets and aerosols of nerve gas.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:14.090
At the same time,

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.250
the presence of larger drops will be quickly revealed

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:22.550
by a color change of the dye indicator.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:28.470
Small metal patches are provided to seal off these spots of gross contamination

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.280
so as to prevent any possibility

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:35.570
of the nerve gas penetrating through the clothing to the skin.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.490
The decontaminant is also applied

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:42.340
to pieces of individual equipment to prevent secondary contamination

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:47.000
which might result from handling the equipment.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:50.630
Blotting cloths are provided for removing any of the liquid agent

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:54.160
which may have splashed on the skin.

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:57.010
The affected skin area is then swabbed

00:18:57.030 --> 00:19:00.050
with a small bag of decontaminating material

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:03.490
which has been moistened with water.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:07.360
The E21 kit can be used to decontaminate mustard

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:09.750
as well as the nerve gases.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:13.020
It is scheduled to undergo final engineering tests

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:17.330
in the fourth quarter of FY60.

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:23.390
No change has been made in the method of impregnating outer garments of protective clothing,

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:28.520
but the protective underwear has been vastly improved over the World War Two type,

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:34.500
which was uncomfortable to wear and often caused skin irritation.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:38.980
Developed in coordination with the Quartermaster Research and Development Center,

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:42.240
it is a soft-textured, lightweight cotton fabric

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:49.800
treated with [hicar?] and gives good protection against liquid toxic agents.

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:54.890
Its protective property is not diminished by perspiration or laundering,

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:58.290
and therefore does not require reimpregnation,

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:03.070
as was the case with the older type.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:06.830
The nearly standardized field protective mask M-17

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.950
is much improved over older types.

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:12.750
Vision and voice transmission are better,

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.180
and having no external canister,

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:19.970
it is streamlined and more comfortable to wear.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:24.860
New special-purpose masks have also been developed.

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:28.460
For the helicopter pilot is the E-75 mask,

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:31.070
which provides unrestricted vision

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:34.580
and is fitted with a special dynamic microphone

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:38.760
for aircraft radio communication.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:43.020
Of similar design is the special mask for armored personnel

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:48.570
with an added feature for the comfort and efficiency of the tank crew.

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:52.440
Provision is made for connecting the individual's canister

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:56.600
to a large central canister in the tank.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:21:00.640
While operating the tank, air is supplied under pressure

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:04.950
from the large canister to the mask of each crew member,

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:08.670
and breathing becomes effortless.

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:12.720
A quick-release connection permits the crew to bail out rapidly

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:16.720
without loss of mask protection.

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:19.470
Still another type of special mask has been developed

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:24.430
for the casualty who is unable to wear his M-17 mask

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:27.400
because of head wounds.

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:30.780
Bag-like in shape, it is made of filter material

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:35.400
and equipped with clear plastic eyepieces.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:39.200
A gas-tight seal is formed by means of a drawstring

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:43.990
which maintains moderate pressure around the neck.

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:46.220
Thus the patient is protected,

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:54.750
while being moved through a toxic atmosphere to an aid station or hospital.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.210
Point-source alarms have been developed to detect

00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:01.750
and automatically warn of the presence of nerve-type chemical agents,

00:22:01.770 --> 00:22:08.260
which in vapor or aerosol form are odorless and invisible.

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:10.720
The larger model on the right has been adopted

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:15.440
by the United States Navy for shipboard use.

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:18.040
The smaller model is a later development

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:22.110
which carries its own power source.

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:25.110
These alarms continuously sample the atmosphere

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.210
through a chemically treated paper.

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:31.010
A concentration of toxic agent in the air,

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:34.410
well below the level required to cause casualties,

00:22:34.430 --> 00:22:37.640
produces a color change on the paper.

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:45.680
This is detected by a photoelectric cell activating the alarm system.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:47.540
Mouth-to-mouth resuscitation

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:51.720
is a newly developed technique of artificial respiration.

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:53.500
In addition to medication,

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:58.820
nerve gas casualties often may require aid in breathing.

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:02.030
With one hand, the operator raises the patient's chin

00:23:02.050 --> 00:23:04.980
to open up his throat and upper airway.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:08.260
With the other hand she holds his nose closed.

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:11.610
Then she takes a deep breath and inflates his lungs,

00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:15.260
just like blowing up a balloon.

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:19.600
The gauge at the upper right registers the percent oxygen saturation

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:24.680
of the blood as measured by an ear oximeter.

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:29.250
Note how it falls off when the worker stops the treatment.

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:33.360
This patient is quite incapable of breathing by himself,

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:35.600
and without artificial respiration,

00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:44.020
the oxygen saturation of his blood soon drops to a low level.

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:50.120
When the treatment is resumed the oximeter reading rapidly returns to normal.

00:23:50.140 --> 00:23:53.950
The basic scientific groundwork for mouth-to-mouth resuscitation

00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:57.030
was performed by the Chemical Warfare Laboratories,

00:23:57.050 --> 00:23:59.340
and the clinical research was conducted

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:05.500
under the auspices of the Army Medical Service at Baltimore City Hospital.

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:13.900
It is expected that this method of artificial respiration will be adopted by the armed forces.

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:30.030
[FOR OFFICIAL USE ONLY]

